	abstract = {Let H and G be two ﬁnite graphs. Deﬁne hH (G) to be the number of homomorphisms from H to G. The function hH (·) extends in a natural way to a function from the set of symmetric matrices to R such that for AG, the adjacency matrix of a graph G, we have hH (AG) = hH (G). Let m be the number of edges of H. It is easy to see that when H is the cycle of length 2n, then hH (·)1/m is the 2n-th Schatten–von Neumann norm. We investigate a question of Lov´asz that asks for a characterization of graphs H for which the function hH (·)1/m is a norm.},
