of size \${\textbackslash}frac\{nd\}\{4\}+{\textbackslash}Omega(n{\textasciicircum}\{5/4\}/{\textbackslash}log n)\$. This is not necessarily true without the assumption of regularity, or the bounds on \$d\$. The positive discrepancy of regular graphs is controlled by the second eigenvalue \${\textbackslash}lambda\_2\$, as \${\textbackslash}mbox\{disc\}{\textasciicircum}\{+\}(G){\textbackslash}leq {\textbackslash}frac\{{\textbackslash}lambda\_2\}\{2\} n+d\$. As a byproduct of our arguments, we present lower bounds on \${\textbackslash}lambda\_2\$ for regular graphs, extending the celebrated Alon-Boppana theorem in the dense regime.},
