	abstract = {The rainbow Tur´an number ex∗(n, H) of a graph H is the maximum possible number of edges in a properly edge-coloured n-vertex graph with no rainbow subgraph isomorphic to H. We prove that for any integer k ≥ 2, ex∗(n, C2k) = O(n1+1/k). This is tight and establishes a conjecture of Keevash, Mubayi, Sudakov and Verstra¨ete. We use the same method to prove several other conjectures in various topics. First, we prove that there exists a constant c such that any properly edge-coloured n-vertex graph with more than cn(log n)4 edges contains a rainbow cycle. It is known that there exist properly edge-coloured n-vertex graphs with Ω(n log n) edges which do not contain any rainbow cycle.},
